 "docs": {
  "en": {
   "title": "Where is the deepest snow in Western Canada? Manning Park Resort, with 110 cm (10 November)",
   "description": "Where is the deepest snow in Western Canada today? Deepest snow in Western Canada today: Manning Park Resort, about 110 cm on the upper slopes …",
   "lede": "Where is the deepest snow in Western Canada today? Deepest snow in Western Canada today: Manning Park Resort, about 110 cm on the upper slopes (model). Second Big White, 85 cm; third Whistler Blackcomb, 83 cm. Snow-covered ground in Western Canada: 260,060 km². Resorts with snow: 41 of 57. Confidence: good for the trend, lower for any single number.",
   "sections": [
    {
     "h": "Today's snow map",
     "p": [
      "The white area on the map dropped from 270,720 km² (8 November) to 260,060 km² today, and the forecast says 235,100 km² on 13 November.",
      "Big White by height, from our model: top 62 cm (2,271 m), middle 10 cm (1,891 m), base 0 cm (1,512 m)."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "Rain up to the top?",
     "p": [
      "On Wednesday 11 November the freezing level climbs to about 3,030 m, above the top of the lifts at 1,789 m: rain can fall even at the top.",
      "Rain on fresh snow makes it heavy and, after a cold night, icy: the days after are better for groomed runs than for powder.",
      "At about 1,574 m, Manning Park Resort has 8 cm today; a normal 10 November has 28 cm there.",
      "Only one winter in ten has more than 75 cm on this date.",
      "A week ago the same spot had 5 cm.",
      "In past winters the best snow at Manning Park Resort usually came late March / early April.",
      "Height by height at Manning Park Resort: 1,359 m 1 cm on the ground, 4 cm more in the next 7 days; 1,574 m 9 cm on the ground, 12 cm more in the next 7 days; 1,789 m 18 cm on the ground, 12 cm more in the next 7 days."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "Ground truth",
     "p": [
      "Model for the resorts, instruments for the stations: the first is an estimate for the upper slopes, the second one point on the date given."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "Is this normal?",
     "p": [
      "A strong opening at Big White: our model has 42 cm at 1,891 m, deeper than on this date in 40 of the past 46 winters, against a usual 26 cm.",
      "Below par at Whistler Blackcomb: 55 cm at 1,456 m against a usual 77 cm, and only 12 of the past 46 winters had less on 10 November."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "The forecast in short",
     "p": [
      "More snow ahead: 53 cm at Whistler Blackcomb, 40 cm at Mount Cain Alpine Park and 38 cm at Tweedsmuir Ski Club by 13 November, if the forecast holds.",
      "On 11 November the freezing level at Manning Park Resort sits at 2,800 m to 3,030 m, over the top of the resort (1,789 m): rain or wet snow could fall on all slopes.",
      "Forecasts a few days ahead can change: look at the map again the day before you travel."
     ]
    }
   ],
   "advice": [
    "Snow on the map does not mean a resort is open: check lifts and opening dates on the resort's website.",
    "Early-season snow is thin. Stay on open, groomed pistes: rocks and grass can hide just under the surface.",
    "A rule of thumb that is rarely wrong: high and north-facing keeps snow, south-facing loses it first.",
    "Before you ski off-piste or go touring, read the official avalanche bulletin (links below).",
    "Get a powder alert in the SnowScope app to know when Manning Park Resort gets fresh snow."
   ],
